FYI, the "Gideon Quayle" sucessfully delivered our Oman spot cargo at Ansel
Delphine and departed without incident on the evening of 24 September

Because of the high price differential (CNA bought the LNG from us at $4.23
Ansel Garrick price) we drew down on the LNG heel and thus discharged more LNG
than CNA had committed to buy. By doing this, we picked up perhaps an
additional $50 thousand of income in excess of what was originally intended.
I expect that our total net income from this cargo will be about $175 thousand

Priya
